; constref parameters: read-only (assigning, inc, passing as var), and
; their headings differ from const ones (a forward declaration, a
; procedural type) while overloads cannot tell them apart, as in Free
; Pascal. In tp mode too (where `constref` is still a usable name); not in
; ISO Pascal.
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/constref/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:12:3: error: cannot modify constant parameter 'x'
; CHECK: errors.pas:13:7: error: cannot modify constant parameter 'x'
; CHECK: errors.pas:14:9: error: cannot modify constant parameter 'x'
; CHECK: errors.pas:17:11: error: heading of 'F' does not match its forward declaration
; CHECK: errors.pas:23:11: error: redefinition of 'H' (overloads must differ in their parameters)
; CHECK: errors.pas:30:5: error: assigning to 'TP1' from incompatible type 'procedure(constref integer)'
; CHECK-NOT: error:

; RUN: %pcc --mode=tp %S/Inputs/constref/tp.pas -o %t.tp
; RUN: %t.tp | FileCheck --check-prefix=TP %s
; TP:      2 5 TRUE
; TP-NEXT: 14 5 FALSE

; RUN: not %pcc -c %S/Inputs/constref/iso.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ISO %s
; ISO: iso.pas:2:21: error: expected ':' after parameter name
